167
00:09:26,108 --> 00:09:28,108
Although...

168
00:09:28,108 --> 00:09:30,108
I'm sure they're more than a little preoccupied

169
00:09:30,108 --> 00:09:32,108
at the moment, trying to find a way

170
00:09:32,108 --> 00:09:34,108
into the palace.

171
00:09:34,108 --> 00:09:36,108
I assume they'll come here after they discover

172
00:09:36,108 --> 00:09:38,108
their friends are dead.

173
00:09:38,108 --> 00:09:40,108
And once they do...

174
00:09:40,108 --> 00:09:42,108
we'll be ready.

175
00:10:10,108 --> 00:10:14,108
That...

176
00:10:14,108 --> 00:10:16,108
is my army.

177
00:10:16,108 --> 00:10:18,108
30,000 slaves we've captured this month.

178
00:10:18,108 --> 00:10:20,108
All human too.

179
00:10:30,108 --> 00:10:32,108
And then there's 70,000 fishmen...

180
00:10:32,108 --> 00:10:34,108
trained in combat.

181
00:10:34,108 --> 00:10:56,108
This...

182
00:10:56,108 --> 00:10:58,108
is madness.

183
00:10:58,108 --> 00:11:00,108
They're all from the fishmen district.

184
00:11:00,108 --> 00:11:02,108
Or can't you tell?

185
00:11:02,108 --> 00:11:04,108
Now behold...

186
00:11:04,108 --> 00:11:06,108
100,000...

187
00:11:06,108 --> 00:11:08,108
United Outlaws!

188
00:11:08,108 --> 00:11:10,108
They're all from the fishmen district.

189
00:11:10,108 --> 00:11:12,108
Or can't you tell?

190
00:11:12,108 --> 00:11:14,108
Now behold...

191
00:11:14,108 --> 00:11:16,108
100,000...

192
00:11:16,108 --> 00:11:18,108
United Outlaws!

193
00:11:18,108 --> 00:11:19,108
99,000!

194
00:11:19,108 --> 00:11:20,108
100,000!

195
00:11:20,108 --> 00:11:21,108
Doada bats bay!

196
00:11:22,108 --> 00:11:24,108
13,000,000!

197
00:11:24,108 --> 00:11:41,808
New

198
00:11:41,808 --> 00:11:56,548
Just outside are women and children, more slaves, although they can't fight.

199
00:11:57,208 --> 00:11:59,568
Well, I'm sure we can find a use for them later.

200
00:12:00,408 --> 00:12:04,868
And they're only the first of many humans we will enslave in the coming days.

201
00:12:04,868 --> 00:12:14,308
But as for you islanders, my men are in need of places to stay, so I expect you all to be accommodating by leaving your homes.

202
00:12:14,668 --> 00:12:19,068
Whether you do that by running away or dropping dead makes no difference to me.

203
00:12:19,548 --> 00:12:25,368
What a pathetic scene. You have no class, like a bunch of rowdy children.

204
00:12:27,048 --> 00:12:32,388
You should quit while you're ahead. Horty, Jones.

205
00:12:32,388 --> 00:12:37,888
It's been a long time, Charlie. Is there a reason you're here?

206
00:12:38,788 --> 00:12:43,408
Yes, I wanted to deliver a message. While you're still at the height of your glory.

207
00:12:44,228 --> 00:12:45,628
What did she just say?

208
00:12:46,408 --> 00:12:53,028
I recently had a vision of the imminent destruction of our island. It was a fate brought on by a single man.

209
00:12:53,548 --> 00:12:59,828
Oh yeah, I guess you could call this destruction. So was it me that you saw in your prophecy?

210
00:12:59,828 --> 00:13:01,828
No.

211
00:13:04,168 --> 00:13:09,888
The man who will destroy Fishman Island is Straw Hat Luffy.

212
00:13:12,328 --> 00:13:13,728
That can't be.

213
00:13:14,188 --> 00:13:18,448
Oh, but I'm afraid it can. That said, I don't know how.

214
00:13:19,228 --> 00:13:21,928
The means, well, there's still a mystery to me.

215
00:13:22,048 --> 00:13:23,808
What exactly's your point?

216
00:13:23,988 --> 00:13:25,728
My point is, it's not you.

217
00:13:25,728 --> 00:13:28,948
Fine. I'll spell it out.

218
00:13:29,608 --> 00:13:35,448
No matter what you think you're accomplishing, the person who decides the fate of this island isn't you.

219
00:13:36,028 --> 00:13:37,128
It's a human.

220
00:13:38,368 --> 00:13:41,668
Hear that? Madam Charlie's visions are always accurate.

221
00:13:41,988 --> 00:13:45,968
Yeah. That means Horty will never be in control of Fishman Island.

222
00:13:46,228 --> 00:13:47,628
No matter what he does.

223
00:13:47,628 --> 00:14:17,608
No matter what he does, he will never be in control of Fishman Island.

224
00:14:17,628 --> 00:14:34,508
Charlie, no!

225
00:14:34,508 --> 00:14:35,388
Charlie, no!

226
00:14:35,648 --> 00:14:36,988
How could he do that?

227
00:14:37,288 --> 00:14:38,568
What a load of crap.

228
00:14:39,228 --> 00:14:40,848
What did you hope to accomplish?

229
00:14:40,848 --> 00:14:41,428
Huh?

230
00:14:42,148 --> 00:14:43,728
Come on, let's hear it!

231
00:14:43,728 --> 00:14:48,728
Charlie, you know I'm nothing like your brother.

232
00:14:48,728 --> 00:14:52,728
It's true. I looked up to him a lot when I was a kid.

233
00:14:52,728 --> 00:14:55,728
That's how everybody was with Arlong back then.

234
00:14:55,728 --> 00:14:59,728
However, that changed when we acquired real power.

235
00:14:59,728 --> 00:15:03,728
We didn't take the name Arlong Pirates out of reverence to him.

236
00:15:03,728 --> 00:15:06,728
All we needed was a flag to rally behind.

237
00:15:06,728 --> 00:15:08,728
A symbol to unite people like us.

238
00:15:08,728 --> 00:15:11,728
And now that symbol has served its purpose,

239
00:15:11,728 --> 00:15:14,728
we have surpassed Arlong in strength and ambition alike.

240
00:15:14,728 --> 00:15:17,728
There's only one man capable of destroying this country

241
00:15:17,728 --> 00:15:20,728
and building something better.

242
00:15:20,728 --> 00:15:22,728
And that's me, you got it?

243
00:15:22,728 --> 00:15:25,728
Otherwise, you wouldn't be here, right?

244
00:15:25,728 --> 00:15:30,728
You see, this is power.

245
00:15:30,728 --> 00:15:35,728
Because my followers have faith in change.

246
00:15:35,728 --> 00:15:38,728
It's taken 10 years, but it's time that we finished

247
00:15:38,728 --> 00:15:41,728
what I began so long ago.

248
00:15:41,728 --> 00:15:43,728
And you know what started it?

249
00:15:43,728 --> 00:15:45,728
The death of Queen Otahime.

250
00:15:45,728 --> 00:15:47,728
Yes, that's right.

251
00:15:47,728 --> 00:15:49,728
I've got a little secret.

252
00:15:49,728 --> 00:15:50,728
Wanna hear?

253
00:15:53,728 --> 00:15:55,728
When she was killed,

254
00:15:55,728 --> 00:15:57,728
the one who shot her...

255
00:15:59,728 --> 00:16:01,728
was me!

256
00:16:07,728 --> 00:16:09,728
That can't be true!

257
00:16:13,728 --> 00:16:14,728
Oh no!

258
00:16:14,728 --> 00:16:15,728
The human!

259
00:16:15,728 --> 00:16:17,728
But what about him?

260
00:16:17,728 --> 00:16:18,728
We saw him!

261
00:16:18,728 --> 00:16:22,728
I can't believe in all these years,

262
00:16:22,728 --> 00:16:24,728
you idiots never figured it out!

263
00:16:24,728 --> 00:16:25,728
Can't ya?

264
00:16:25,728 --> 00:16:26,728
The day before,

265
00:16:26,728 --> 00:16:28,728
I had made a deal.

266
00:16:30,728 --> 00:16:32,728
I got no clue who you are.

267
00:16:32,728 --> 00:16:34,728
I don't really care.

268
00:16:34,728 --> 00:16:36,728
As long as you got the money to pay me,

269
00:16:36,728 --> 00:16:38,728
I'll do whatever it is you want.

270
00:16:41,728 --> 00:16:43,728
That's what I'm talking about!

271
00:16:43,728 --> 00:16:45,728
Consider this a down payment.

272
00:16:45,728 --> 00:16:46,728
I'll give you the other half

273
00:16:46,728 --> 00:16:48,728
after you finish the job.

274
00:16:48,728 --> 00:16:49,728
Mister,

275
00:16:49,728 --> 00:16:51,728
you have yourself a deal.

276
